1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:11,861
The internet of things, a phrase Kevin Ashton coined in nineteen ninety nine, connects physical objects fitted with sensors and software so they exchange data and can be controlled remotely.

2
00:00:11,861 --> 00:00:13,528
It has four layers.

3
00:00:13,528 --> 00:00:15,833
Perception: the sensors.

4
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:18,580
Network: the gateway and the link.

5
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:21,432
Processing: the cloud that decides.

6
00:00:21,432 --> 00:00:24,401
Application: the app the farmer sees.

7
00:00:24,401 --> 00:00:31,276
Its weakest point is security: cheap devices shipped with default passwords have been hijacked into botnets.

